        "question": {
          ":question/id": "3293b225-0b3c-58f0-9442-428938c3eec7",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices that are in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & -8 & -1 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied). \n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & -8 & -1 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ have coefficient matrices that are in row echelon form.",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
